DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt() function will initialize _l_o_c_k to an unlocked
     state and allocate any resources necessary to begin using it.  If _p_s_h_a_r_e_d
     is set to PTHREAD_PROCESS_SHARED, any thread, whether belonging to the
     process in which the spinlock was created or not, that has access to the
     memory area where _l_o_c_k resides, can use _l_o_c_k.  If it is set to
     PTHREAD_PROCESS_PRIVATE, it can only be used by threads within the same
     process.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ddeessttrrooyy() function will destroy _l_o_c_k and release any re‐
     sources that may have been allocated on its behalf.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, both pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt() and pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ddeessttrrooyy() will
     return zero.  Otherwise, an error number will be returned to indicate the
     error.

     Neither of these functions will return EINTR.

EERRRROORRSS
     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt() and pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ddeessttrrooyy() functions will fail
     if:

     [EBUSY]            An attempt to initialize or destroy _l_o_c_k while it is
                        in use.

     [EINVAL]           The value specified by _l_o_c_k is invalid.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt() function will fail if:

     [EAGAIN]           Insufficient resources, other than memory, to initial‐
                        ize _l_o_c_k.

     [ENOMEM]           Insufficient memory to initialize _l_o_c_k.

